# Raw-shaped doc-IR of the TI MSP430FR2355's Table 4-1 "Pin Attributes", from SLASEC4D (May 2018,
# revised December 2019), pages 18 and 20. The tables are the docling output for those pages,
# unedited; the pages' other content and page 19 are left out.
#
# It is a FIXTURE, not a corpus entry. The PDF and the full doc-IR stay outside this repo.
#
# One row per signal, several rows to a pin, numbered in four packages (PT, RHA, DBT, RSM). The
# reset-state column is filled on each pin's first row. The awkward cases it carries, all real:
#
#   - A DESIGNATOR ON A MIDDLE ROW. Page 18 puts pin 1's DBT number (5) on its fourth row with no
#     span, and page 20 puts P1.7's numbers on its fifth row (TDO), the vertical middle of the
#     merged cells.
#   - A SPAN RUNNING OVER THE NEXT PIN. Page 20's RHA 24 spans eleven rows, P2.0's three and
#     P1.7's eight.
#   - "N/A" AS A RESET STATE, on the supply pins DVCC and DVSS, which starts a pin like "OFF".
#   - TWO DASHES MERGED INTO ONE CELL ("- -") on P1.6's TCLK row, which does not start a pin.
#   - A RESET CELL ON THE WRONG ROW. Page 18 prints "OFF" against XOUT and leaves P2.5's empty,
#     so P2.5 is read as part of a pin named XOUT. A patch is the fix for this one.
#   - TWO PINS' SIGNALS IN ONE CELL ("P5.4 (RD) P5.3 (RD)") at the foot of page 20, gapped as a
#     possible boundary.
